      "direction": "Directions for questions 1 to 25: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.",
      "text": "In 802.3 LAN the Bandwidth of the cable is 5 Mbps, velocity of propagation is 2.1 × 10^8 m/s, length of LAN is 2.1 km, what is the minimum packet size?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "100 bits"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "120 bits"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "210 bits"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "115 bits"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "100 bits",
      "explanation": "Condition for minimum packet size in Ethernet:\nTransmission delay = round trip delay\n\n2 × L / B = 2 × d / v\n\n2 × L / (5 × 10^6) = 2 × (2.1 × 10^3 m) / (2.1 × 10^8)\n\nL = 100 bits. Choice (A)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Computer Networks",
      "topic": "Data link layer / Ethernet",
      "subtopic": "Minimum Ethernet frame size",
      "tags": []
